        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0182" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/654</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-21T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 21, 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6509. Confidential to Secretary and President:</p>
                <p>The Prime Minister asked me to breakfast this morning to discuss the desirability
                    of trying to induce Austria and especially Bulgaria to make separate peace, but
                    his conclusion is that under present conditions any effort would be premature in
                    this matter. Coming events in Russia play so large a part that it seems better
                    to wait and see whether Russia will again show important military activity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
